Z||000003||pherder||03-05-2000||02:48 PM||||Kevin,<P>The Quad 4s look to be a very nice package ... low weight (aluminum head), multi valve, dual cams, good gas mileage (if you keep a light foot) and HOs have 175-195 HP (depending on year/cams).<P>The problems are they can't keep head gaskets from failing so be prepared to change it out when it goes (notice, I wrote, "when" not "if"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Having said that, I am finishing up my second Quad 4 into a Fiero swap.  First one was a head gasket blowing fool  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  Replace the head gasket twice and sold it soon after.  It was an 89 engine which they had the most problems with (87-89).  The HO came out in 89 and was discontinued in 1993-4.  The 89-92 HO heads were the best for HP.<P>The problems I have run into SO FAR have been:  <P>No real "kit" to install into an 88 (had the mounts made for me, custom).<P>I didn't get a complete assembly so I have been mixing a matching parts from any Quad 4 car (to include the newer TwinCam versions).  I would recomend that you get the ENTIRE front clip assembly off a donor car to insure you get EVERYTHING you need that is Quad 4 unique.<P>The early Getrag/Muncie 5 speeds are more like the Getrag/Muncie 5 speeds in the Fiero.  You will still need Rodney Dickman's shifter conversion kit to make it shift in the Fiero.  Later models DO NOT HAVE the mounting bosses for the Fiero's mounting brackets (shifter cable or the mounts to the engine cradle!) so some creative mounts will have to be made.<P>The later Getrag/Muncie's have a throwout bearing that is also the slave cylinder!  Or you will get one that has a external slave that bolts directly to the bellhousing and pushes an internal arm.  So far I haven't been able to make the Fiero's clutch master cylinder work with those types of slave cylinders.  I will do what another Quad 4 Fiero owner has done and install a Wilwood master cylinder (7/8") and plumb that to the slave.<P>Wiring was fun to mate together ... haven't had a chance to see if my wiring works, yet.<P>Coolant connections have been fun ... not.<P>Etc., etc., etc. ...<P>Paul||||reg||11
